+## 11. Error Handling Design
+
+### Error Response Format (RFC 7807)
+
+All error responses use `application/problem+json`:
+
+```json
+{
+    "type": "/problems/report-type-unknown",
+    "title": "Unknown Report Type",
+    "status": 422,
+    "detail": "Report type 'INVALID_TYPE' is not registered. Available types: ['ALLOWED_ITEM_TYPES']",
+    "instance": "/api/v1/reports/requests"
+}
+```
+
+### Error Catalog
+
+| Error | HTTP | `type` URI | Trigger |
+|-------|------|-----------|---------|
+| Unknown report type | 422 | `/problems/report-type-unknown` | `report_type` not in registry |
+| Validation error | 422 | `/problems/validation-error` | Pydantic rejects request body |
+| Report not found | 404 | `/problems/report-not-found` | `request_id` not in database |
+| Document not available | 404 | `/problems/document-not-found` | No document row for this request |
+| Document too large | 410 | `/problems/document-too-large` | `storage_status = DOCUMENT_TOO_LARGE` |
+| Target API error | 502 | `/problems/target-api-error` | Target returned non-2xx on create/poll |
+| Internal error | 500 | `/problems/internal-error` | Unhandled exception |
+
+### Logging on Error
+
+| Context Field | Always Logged | Never Exposed to Caller |
+|--------------|---------------|------------------------|
+| `report_request_id` | Yes | — |
+| `report_type` | Yes | — |
+| `target_request_id` | Yes | — |
+| `error_class` | Yes | — |
+| `error_message` | Yes (sanitized) | — |
+| Stack trace | Yes (to logs) | Never in HTTP response |
+| `tgtrt` value | **Never** | **Never** |
+| `Authorization` value | **Never** | **Never** |
+| `download_url` | Yes (may contain tokens) | Not in error response |
+
+### Fallback Behavior
+
+| Dependency | Unavailable Behavior | Rationale |
+|------------|---------------------|-----------|
+| Postgres | Fail-closed (503) | Cannot persist state; unsafe to proceed |
+| Target API | Fail-closed (502) | Cannot create/poll report; retry is caller's responsibility |
+| `registry.yaml` | Fail-closed (startup crash) | No types = no purpose; fail loudly |
+
