+# Security Review — STORY-017: Target Async Reports Framework
+
+**Phase:** 6b — Security Review
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Reviewer:** Phase 6b Security Architect
+**Scope:** Medium
+**Status:** APPROVED with conditions
+
+---
+
+## 1. Credential Handling
+
+### `tgtrt` Header (R-A-3 — MANDATORY)
+
+The `tgtrt` header is a session/auth credential required for downloading report documents from Target. It is treated as a secret with the same sensitivity as `Authorization` bearer tokens.
+
+**Controls implemented:**
+
+| Control | Implementation | Verified |
+|---------|---------------|----------|
+| Never logged | `_redact_auth_on_log` httpx event hook strips `tgtrt` before debug logging | `test_tgtrt_redacted.py` (4 tests) |
+| Never in error responses | RFC 7807 error handler does not include request headers | Router inspection |
+| Never in persisted records | `tgtrt` is not stored in `report_requests` or `report_documents` tables | Schema inspection |
+| Test fixtures use placeholder | All tests use `"test-tgtrt-value"` — never a real credential | Code review |
+| Redaction covers all sensitive headers | `authorization`, `tgtrt`, `x-api-key` all redacted by same hook | `test_redact_hook_modifies_headers_in_place` |
+
+**Residual risk:** The `tgtrt` provisioning model (OQ-2) is not yet defined. If `tgtrt` is a long-lived static token, rotation procedures must be documented before production. If it's session-based, expiry/refresh logic is needed.
+
+### Authorization Header
+
+Same redaction controls as `tgtrt`. Bearer token stripped by `_redact_auth_on_log` hook.
+
+---
+
+## 2. PII Assessment
+
+### Report Payload PII Risk
+
+**Classification: UNKNOWN — requires review before production use.**
+
+Target report payloads (e.g., `ALLOWED_ITEM_TYPES`) may contain:
+
+| Data Category | PII Risk | Mitigation |
+|--------------|----------|------------|
+| Item TCINs | No PII — product identifiers | No action needed |
+| Seller identifiers | Low PII — business entity IDs | Acceptable for operational storage |
+| Customer data | **Unknown** — Amazon reports can contain customer PII; Target reports may too | `pii_reviewed` flag gates production use |
+| Pricing data | No PII — commercial data | No action needed |
+| Order data (if future report types) | **High PII risk** — names, addresses, phone numbers | Must NOT be stored in JSONB without encryption |
+
+**Hard gate:** The `pii_reviewed` boolean on `report_documents` defaults to `false`. Production workflows MUST NOT expose report content to end users until `pii_reviewed = true` is set by a human reviewer for each report type.
+
+### PII Mitigation Controls
+
+1. **`pii_reviewed` flag:** Default `false` on all `report_documents` rows. Must be explicitly set `true` per report type after human review confirms PII classification.
+2. **`retention_expires_at`:** Enables time-based deletion of report content. NULL default (no auto-delete) but infrastructure is in place for retention policies.
+3. **JSONB storage:** Content is queryable but not encrypted at rest. If PII is confirmed in any report type, encryption-at-rest must be added before that type is enabled in production.
+4. **No content in error responses:** Report content is never included in HTTP error responses or log messages.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Network Security
+
+| Concern | Assessment |
+|---------|-----------|
+| Outbound HTTP scope | Client only calls Target report endpoints (POST create, GET poll, GET download) |
+| No inbound from Target | Target does not call back to our API; all communication is client-initiated |
+| TLS | httpx uses system TLS by default; Target endpoints are HTTPS-only |
+| DNS | No custom DNS resolution; standard system resolver |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Input Validation
+
+| Input | Validation | Risk |
+|-------|-----------|------|
+| `report_type` in POST body | Validated against YAML registry; rejected with 422 if unknown | Low — config-driven allowlist |
+| `extra` fields in POST body | Rejected by Pydantic `extra="forbid"` | Low |
+| Target response `status` | Passthrough to `status_raw`; unknown values → `UNRECOGNIZED_STATUS` | Low — defensive parsing |
+| Downloaded report content | Parsed as JSON; size-gated by `MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES` (10MB) | Medium — large payloads rejected safely |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Conditions for Production Use
+
+- [ ] **PII review per report type:** Before enabling any report type in production, a human must review sample payloads and set `pii_reviewed = true` if no PII is present, or add encryption if PII is confirmed.
+- [ ] **`tgtrt` provisioning model defined:** OQ-2 must be resolved — rotation, expiry, and secure storage procedures documented.
+- [ ] **Retention policy activated:** `retention_expires_at` must be set for all report types storing content, per data governance requirements.
+
+---
+
+*Produced by Phase 6b Security Review, STORY-017. No HTTP calls made. All assessments based on feature-spec.md design and Target OpenAPI documentation.*
