+# Test Design — STORY-017: Target Async Reports Framework
+
+**Phase:** 7 — Test Design
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Scope:** Medium
+**Status:** RED state confirmed — 66 FAILED, 2 PASSED, 0 ERRORS (68 total)
+**Advance type:** confirm (requires human approval before Phase 8)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Overview
+
+This document covers the test design for STORY-017's Approach A implementation: asyncio in-process poller + Postgres JSONB + YAML registry. Tests target all four domain modules (Client, Lifecycle, Registry, Storage) plus the FastAPI API layer and two mandatory security gates.
+
+All tests are in **RED state**: stubs in `app/reports/` raise `NotImplementedError`. Every test fails for the right reason — implementation is absent, not test infrastructure.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Test Coverage Map
+
+| Domain | File | Tests | Acceptance Criteria |
+|--------|------|-------|---------------------|
+| Registry | `test_registry.py` | 14 | SC-3 (YAML config), startup safety |
+| Client | `test_client.py` | 14 | SC-1 (lifecycle HTTP), SC-2 (tgtrt redaction) |
+| Lifecycle | `test_lifecycle.py` | 15 | SC-1 (state machine), R-A-2, R-A-4, R-A-10 |
+| API Endpoints | `test_api_endpoints.py` | 12 | SC-1 (API surface), RFC 7807 errors |
+| tgtrt Redaction | `test_tgtrt_redacted.py` | 4 | **SC-2, R-A-3 (MANDATORY Gate)** |
+| No Production Calls | `test_no_production_calls.py` | 4 | **SC-4, Gate 2a (MANDATORY Gate)** |
+| **Total** | — | **68** | — |
+
+**Coverage target:** 70% (per `config.yaml`). Phase 8 must not fall below this.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Mandatory Security Gates
+
+These two gates are **non-negotiable** per CLAUDE.md External API Write Safety policy and feature-spec.md SC-2/SC-4:
+
+### Gate 2a: No Production HTTP Calls (`test_no_production_calls.py`)
+
+| Test | Assertion |
+|------|-----------|
+| `test_create_request_does_not_call_production` | `create_report_request` uses mock transport only |
+| `test_get_request_does_not_call_production` | `get_report_request` uses mock transport only |
+| `test_download_report_does_not_call_production` | `download_report` uses mock transport only |
+| `test_unmatched_call_raises_not_silently_succeeds` | Unregistered routes raise (respx strict default) |
+
+All four tests use `@respx.mock` — any unmatched real network call will raise `httpx.ConnectError`.
+
+### Gate 2b: tgtrt Credential Redaction (`test_tgtrt_redacted.py`)
+
+| Test | Assertion |
+|------|-----------|
+| `test_tgtrt_absent_from_logged_request_headers` | `tgtrt` value absent from `caplog.text` after download |
+| `test_authorization_token_absent_from_logged_request_headers` | Bearer token absent from `caplog.text` after API call |
+| `test_redact_hook_modifies_headers_in_place` | `_redact_auth_on_log` sets sensitive headers to `***REDACTED***` |
+| `test_tgtrt_sent_on_wire_but_not_in_logs` | tgtrt IS present on wire (download works) but NOT in logs |
+
+The last test (`test_tgtrt_sent_on_wire_but_not_in_logs`) distinguishes "header stripped for logs" from "header not sent at all" — both redaction AND delivery must be correct.
+
+**IMPORTANT for Phase 8:** The string `"test-tgtrt-value"` is the only value used in test fixtures. Real `tgtrt` credentials MUST NEVER appear in any test file, fixture, or committed value.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Registry Tests (`test_registry.py`)
+
+### Design rationale
+
+The YAML registry is SC-3's canonical implementation — "new report type = config change, not code change." Tests verify the full load/read/extend lifecycle.
+
+### Test classes
+
+| Class | Tests | What is verified |
+|-------|-------|-----------------|
+| `TestLoadRegistry` | 6 | File loading, Pydantic validation, default values, default path, missing file, bad YAML |
+| `TestGetRegistry` | 2 | Error when not loaded, returns registry after load |
+| `TestListTypes` | 2 | Returns names, all strings |
+| `TestGetTypeConfig` | 3 | Known type → config, unknown → ValueError, error lists available types |
+| `TestRegisterType` | 3 | Adds new type, idempotent on duplicate, retrievable after add |
+
+### Notable test: `test_raises_if_not_loaded`
+
+```python
+def test_raises_if_not_loaded(self):
+    import app.reports.registry as reg_module
+    reg_module._REGISTRY = None
+    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match="not loaded"):
+        get_registry()
+```
+
+This verifies the startup guard: if `load_registry()` was never called, `get_registry()` must raise `RuntimeError` with "not loaded" in the message. Phase 8 must implement this exactly.
+
+### Fixture: `reset_registry`
+
+An `autouse=True` fixture resets `_REGISTRY` to its prior value after each test. This prevents test pollution when the global `_REGISTRY` singleton is mutated.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Client Tests (`test_client.py`)
+
+### Design rationale
+
+`TargetReportsClient` is the only module that touches the network. All tests use `@respx.mock` — no real HTTP calls. Tests verify URL construction, request body shape, header presence, and error propagation.
+
+### Test classes
+
+| Class | Tests | What is verified |
+|-------|-------|-----------------|
+| `TestCreateReportRequest` | 5 | URL format, body fields, optional dates, date absence, non-2xx raises |
+| `TestGetReportRequest` | 2 | URL format, 404 raises |
+| `TestDownloadReport` | 3 | URL, tgtrt header sent, 4xx/5xx raises |
+| `TestRedactAuthOnLog` | 4 | Authorization stripped, tgtrt stripped, x-api-key stripped, non-sensitive preserved |
+
+### Key assertion: `test_sends_tgtrt_header`
+
+```python
+route = respx.get(download_url).mock(...)
+await async_client.download_report(download_url)
+sent_headers = route.calls[0].request.headers
+assert "tgtrt" in sent_headers
+```
+
+Verifies the tgtrt header is actually sent on the wire during download (not accidentally removed by the redaction hook before wire transmission).
+
+### Key assertion: `test_redact_strips_tgtrt`
+
+```python
+request = httpx.Request("GET", "...", headers={"tgtrt": "real-tgtrt-credential-value"})
+await TargetReportsClient._redact_auth_on_log(request)
+assert request.headers["tgtrt"] == "***REDACTED***"
+```
+
+Verifies in-place mutation. Phase 8 must set the header value to exactly `"***REDACTED***"`.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Lifecycle Tests (`test_lifecycle.py`)
+
+### Design rationale
+
+`ReportLifecycleService` is the state machine core. Tests use `AsyncMock(spec=ReportStorage)` and `AsyncMock(spec=TargetReportsClient)` — no real DB or HTTP. `asyncio.sleep` is patched to prevent actual delays.
+
+### Test classes
+
+| Class | Tests | State machine path tested |
+|-------|-------|--------------------------|
+| `TestRequestReport` | 3 | Create → return UUID; validate type; client call args |
+| `TestPollAndComplete` | 6 | COMPLETE→DONE; FAILED→FAILED; unknown→UNRECOGNIZED; status_raw stored; timeout→FAILED; attempt counting |
+| `TestHandleDownload` | 6 | Success→DONE; no URL→FAILED; HTTP error→FAILED; oversized→DOCUMENT_TOO_LARGE; null content; stored content |
+| `TestStartupSweep` | 3 | Re-enqueue count; zero when none; 60s threshold |
+
+### Critical test: R-A-4 mitigation
+
+```python
+async def test_returns_unrecognized_on_unknown_status(self, ...):
+    mock_client.get_report_request.return_value = {"status": "MYSTERY_STATUS_42"}
+    ...
+    result = await lifecycle.poll_and_complete(sample_request_id)
+    assert result == UNRECOGNIZED_STATUS
+```
+
+Any status not in `TARGET_SUCCESS_STATUSES` ∪ `TARGET_FAILURE_STATUSES` ∪ `{"PENDING"}` must produce `UNRECOGNIZED_STATUS` without crashing. The poller must not raise on unknown enum values.
+
+### Critical test: R-A-10 mitigation
+
+```python
+async def test_returns_document_too_large_when_oversized(self, ...):
+    oversized_content = b"x" * (MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES + 1)
+    mock_client.download_report.return_value = oversized_content
+    result = await lifecycle._handle_download(...)
+    assert result == DOCUMENT_TOO_LARGE
+```
+
+### Critical test: R-A-2 mitigation (startup sweep)
+
+```python
+async def test_queries_stale_with_60s_threshold(self, ...):
+    await lifecycle.startup_sweep()
+    mock_storage.get_stale_requests.assert_called_once_with(stale_threshold_seconds=60)
+```
+
+Phase 8 must call `get_stale_requests(stale_threshold_seconds=60)` exactly — not 59, not 61.
+
+### Patching strategy
+
+`asyncio.sleep` is patched in all `poll_and_complete` tests to prevent real delays. `get_type_config` is patched to return `_make_type_config()` directly — tests do not depend on the registry being loaded.
+
+---
+
+## 7. API Endpoint Tests (`test_api_endpoints.py`)
+
+### Design rationale
+
+Uses FastAPI `TestClient` (synchronous). Tests mock the router's DI providers (`get_lifecycle_service`, `get_storage`, `get_registry`). The router stub raises `NotImplementedError` for all endpoints — every test fails in RED state.
+
+### Test classes
+
+| Class | Tests | HTTP behavior verified |
+|-------|-------|----------------------|
+| `TestPostReportRequest` | 5 | 201 valid, 422 unknown type, 422 extra fields, RFC 7807 shape, 502 on Target error |
+| `TestGetReportRequest` | 2 | 200 existing, 404 missing |
+| `TestGetReportDocument` | 3 | 200 stored, 404 no doc, 410 too large |
+| `TestListReportTypes` | 2 | 200 list, required fields |
+
+### RFC 7807 assertion
+
+Phase 8 must return `application/problem+json` on all error responses. The 422 test asserts that the response body contains at minimum `"type"` or `"detail"` — Phase 8 should return a full RFC 7807 body with `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`.
+
+### Phase 8 DI requirement
+
+The router must expose three injectable providers:
+- `get_lifecycle_service()` → `ReportLifecycleService`
+- `get_storage()` → `ReportStorage`
+- `get_registry()` → list of `ReportTypeConfig`
+
+These are patched in tests via `patch("app.reports.router.<function_name>")`.
+
+---
+
+## 8. State Machine Coverage Summary
+
+| State | Covered by | Test |
+|-------|-----------|------|
+| `PENDING` → `DONE` | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_done_on_complete_status` |
+| `PENDING` → `FAILED` (Target failure) | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_failed_on_target_failure` |
+| `PENDING` → `FAILED` (timeout) | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_failed_on_timeout` |
+| `PENDING` → `UNRECOGNIZED_STATUS` | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_unrecognized_on_unknown_status` |
+| `DOWNLOADING` → `DONE` | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_done_on_successful_download` |
+| `DOWNLOADING` → `FAILED` (no URL) | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_failed_when_no_download_url` |
+| `DOWNLOADING` → `FAILED` (HTTP error) | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_failed_on_download_http_error` |
+| `DOWNLOADING` → `DOCUMENT_TOO_LARGE` | `test_lifecycle.py` | `test_returns_document_too_large_when_oversized` |
+
+---
+
+## 9. Risk Mitigations Tested
+
+| Risk | Spec section | Test |
+|------|-------------|------|
+| R-A-2: restart drops in-flight polls | §5 Startup Sweep | `TestStartupSweep.*` (3 tests) |
+| R-A-3: tgtrt in logs | §6 Credential Redaction | `TestTgtrtRedactedInLogs.*` (4 tests) |
+| R-A-4: unknown status crashes poller | §5 State Machine | `test_returns_unrecognized_on_unknown_status`, `test_stores_status_raw_on_unrecognized` |
+| R-A-10: oversized payload | §7 Lifecycle | `test_returns_document_too_large_when_oversized`, `test_document_too_large_stores_null_content` |
+
+---
+
+## 10. Test Infrastructure
+
+### Pytest configuration
+
+```ini
+# pytest.ini (created in Phase 7)
+[pytest]
+asyncio_mode = auto
+testpaths = tests
+```
+
+`asyncio_mode = auto` enables all async test functions and async fixtures without per-test `@pytest.mark.asyncio` decoration.
+
+### Packages required
+
+All installed in `.venv` as of Phase 7:
+
+| Package | Version | Use |
+|---------|---------|-----|
+| `pytest` | 9.0.3 | Test runner |
+| `pytest-asyncio` | 1.3.0 | Async test support |
+| `httpx` | 0.28.1 | HTTP client + TestClient transport |
+| `respx` | 0.23.1 | HTTP mock router (Gate 2a) |
+| `pydantic` | 2.13.3 | Registry + model validation |
+| `pyyaml` | 6.0.3 | YAML parsing |
+| `fastapi` | 0.136.1 | API framework + TestClient |
+| `starlette` | 1.0.0 | ASGI core |
+
+### Stub module structure
+
+Phase 8 will replace stubs with real implementations. Stub files created:
+
+```
+app/
+├── __init__.py
+├── main.py                  # FastAPI app + router include
+└── reports/
+    ├── __init__.py
+    ├── registry.yaml        # Production YAML (ALLOWED_ITEM_TYPES)
+    ├── registry.py          # Stub → all functions raise NotImplementedError
+    ├── client.py            # Stub → all methods raise NotImplementedError
+    ├── storage.py           # Stub → all methods raise NotImplementedError
+    ├── lifecycle.py         # Stub → all methods raise NotImplementedError
+    ├── models.py            # Real Pydantic models (Phase 7 complete)
+    └── router.py            # Stub → all endpoints raise NotImplementedError
+```
+
+### Mock patterns
+
+| Object | How mocked | Rationale |
+|--------|-----------|-----------|
+| `ReportStorage` | `AsyncMock(spec=ReportStorage)` | Avoids real DB; spec ensures method names are correct |
+| `TargetReportsClient` | `AsyncMock(spec=TargetReportsClient)` | Avoids real HTTP; spec ensures method names are correct |
+| `httpx` outbound | `@respx.mock` | Intercepts all outbound HTTP in test scope |
